title: "VROOM-SBI: Simulation-Based Inference for Rotation Measure Synthesis"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-05-14
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/arpan-52/vroom-sbi"

authors:
  - family-names: Pal
    given-names: Arpan
    affiliation: "National Radio Astronomy Observatory; National Centre for Radio Astrophysics"
  - family-names: Jagannathan
    given-names: Preshanth
    affiliation: "National Radio Astronomy Observatory"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2112-2163"

abstract: >
  VROOM-SBI performs Bayesian inference on Faraday rotation measures from
  polarized radio spectra (Q and U as functions of frequency) using
  simulation-based inference with pre-trained neural posterior estimators.
  Given observed Q(lambda^2) and U(lambda^2) spectra, it returns full
  posterior probability distributions over Faraday depth structure without
  requiring likelihood evaluations or classical QU-fitting.

keywords:
  - radio astronomy
  - polarimetry
  - rotation measure synthesis
  - simulation-based inference
  - neural posterior estimation
  - Faraday rotation

